{"name":"White City","hex":"#d6d0cc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"White City","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A neighbourhood around Wood Lane, Shepherd's Bush, borough of Hammersmith and Fulham, Greater London, England .","A town in the Rural Municipality of Edenwold, Saskatchewan, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/White_City"}],"entries":[{"title":"White City, Perth","blocks":[{"text":"White City, also known as Cooee City or Ugly Land, was an amusement park that existed on the Perth foreshore in Perth, Western Australia between World War I and 1929."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_City%2C_Perth","wikidata":"Q7994548"},{"title":"White City railway station","blocks":[{"text":"White City was a railway station on the St Albans line on the Melbourne rail network. It was located approximately 700 metres (2,300 ft) west of Tottenham station in the suburb of Tottenham."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/White_City_1930.png/330px-White_City_1930.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_City_railway_station","wikidata":"Q7994563"},{"title":"White City (Chicago)","blocks":[{"text":"White City was a recreational area located in the Greater Grand Crossing and Woodlawn community areas on the south side of Chicago from 1905 until the 1950s. At the time of its opening, on May 26, 1905, it was claimed to be the largest park of its type in the United States. It contributed to Chicago's status as the city with the most amusement parks in the United States until 1908. It eventually introduced the world to the Goodyear Blimp, which was first assembled at the park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/C1905_White_City_under_construction.jpg/330px-C1905_White_City_under_construction.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_City_(Chicago)","wikidata":"Q7994550"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City","wikidata":"Q515"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/White_City_At_Night.jpg/330px-White_City_At_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/White_City_At_Night.jpg/330px-White_City_At_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite_City_At_Night.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/White_City_Ballroom.jpg/330px-White_City_Ballroom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3